---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DocumentCard from '../components/DocumentCard.astro';
import { portalDocuments } from '../lib/registry.ts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Open Journal Systems at ICJIA — documentation"
  description="Working documents for the ICJIA Open Journal Systems test server: what it is, how it was built, and how the preprint server beside it differs."
>
  <main class="page" id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="masthead">
      <h1>Open Journal Systems, on trial at ICJIA</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A test server is running. One document covers whether to keep it, one covers running the
        journal day to day, one covers how the server was built, and one covers the preprint server
        installed beside it — what it is, and how it differs from both the journal and the Research
        Hub.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="shelf">
      {portalDocuments.map((doc) => <DocumentCard doc={doc} />)}
    </div>

    <footer class="colophon">
      <p>
        These documents are drafts, and the server they describe is temporary. Nothing published on
        it is permanent.
      </p>
      <p>
        They are written from a close reading of the official Open Journal Systems and Open Preprint
        Systems documentation, and from a working test installation — not from experience of running
        either system in production. <strong>Expect some of this to be wrong, and some of it to go out
        of date.</strong> That is the nature of a document written while the thing it describes is
        still being decided. If you find something incorrect, unclear, or no longer true, say so —
        every page carries a link for it, and corrections are wanted rather than merely tolerated.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
